<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills. [corrected 05:55 gmt]</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 182-day T-bills. [corrected 05:55 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 9.050 (corrects from 9.950) percent from 9.029 percent at the previous auction on May 26.</p>
<p>The new bills, with a value of 1,444.925 million pounds, replace bills worth 991 million maturing on Tuesday. The treasury had asked for 1.3 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: December 2, 1997 (Nov 25, 1997).</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.950 percent (9.029).</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,444.925 million (1,312.3 million).</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,644.925 million (1,432.300 million).</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.500-9.450 percent (8.000-9.496).</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.500-10.200 percent (8.000-10.200).</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 180 (125).</p>
<p>Number of bids: 188 (127).</p>
<p>($1 = 3.395 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
